  "why": "BUG-012 scope 02. The reversal fixture pins a cutoff; the cutoff used to resolve against data/bars/*.json, which the scheduled refresh rewrites. A committed test therefore had an input no commit controlled, and 643d74bfd turned it deterministically red. These rows are the resolved inputs, committed: changing them takes a reviewed commit to this file. Each symbol carries the row before the cutoff, the row the cutoff resolves to, and the row after it, so the loader's t <= cutoff filter is still exercised on both edges rather than trivially satisfied by a single row. Corpus coherence is not left unguarded by this pin: scope 01's scripts/validate-bars-coherence.mjs scans every published row repo-wide, and scripts/validate-agenda-fixture-pin.mjs reports when the corpus row behind a pin changes.",
